    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thought and tangible problem-solving—something I’ve always found both challenging and deeply rewarding. As someone who studied it rigorously in academia, it’s not just a tool but a language that shapes how I approach logic and creativity. Though my personality leans toward openness (low) and agreeableness (high), math demands precision, which aligns with my conscientiousness. It’s both intimidating and exhilarating, like learning an instrument where every note matters.",
